                                            <physDesc>
                                                <ab type="codicological-definition">
                                                    <objectType style="codex">Single manuscript</objectType>
                                                </ab>
                                                <objectDesc>
                                                    <supportDesc>
                                                        <support>
                                                            <material>Paper</material>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental paper, except ff. 356-359 remade in Western paper

BnF EAD physical description (srcphys_05842e50053246506965e0): 14 à 15 lignes à la page. Surface écrite 190 × 120 mm.Papier oriental (sauf les fol. 356-359 refaits en papier occidental).360 fol.Écriture orientale (Égypte). Texte en partie vocalisé. — Premiers mots des chapitres en hébreu écrit en caractères samaritains.Invocation au centre d&apos;une page ornée de dessins géométriques à l&apos;encre rouge et noire (f. 1 v).270 × 180 mm.Reliure du XVIIe s., maroquin rouge. Monogramme de Peiresc et filets estampés à chaud.</note>
                                                        </support>
                                                        <extent>
                                                            <measure unit="folio">360 folios</measure>
                                                            <dimensions>
                                                                <height unit="mm">270</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">180</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </extent>
                                                    </supportDesc>
                                                    <layoutDesc>
                                                        <summary>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">14-15 lines per page.</note>
                                                        </summary>
                                                        <layout writtenLines="14-15" columns="1" xml:id="layout-1">
                                                            <dimensions type="written">
                                                                <height unit="mm">190</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">120</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </layout>
                                                    </layoutDesc>
                                                </objectDesc>
                                                <handDesc>
                                                    <summary xml:lang="en">Eastern Arabic hand, described as Egyptian. Text partly vocalized. First words of chapters are in Hebrew written in Samaritan characters.</summary>
                                                </handDesc>
                                                <scriptDesc>
                                                    <scriptNote script="arabic">
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Legacy hand scope: major.</note>
                                                    </scriptNote>
                                                </scriptDesc>
                                                <decoDesc>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Invocation at the center of a page decorated with geometric drawings in red and black ink at f. 1v.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                </decoDesc>
                                                <bindingDesc>
                                                    <binding>
                                                        <decoNote>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">17th-century red morocco binding with Peiresc monogram and fillets stamped in gold.</note>
                                                        </decoNote>
                                                    </binding>
                                                </bindingDesc>
                                            </physDesc>
                                            <history>
                                                <summary>BnF EAD catalogue (srcphys_05842e50053246506965e0): Pentateuque, à l&apos;usage des Samaritains. Date described in the BnF catalogue: 1433.</summary>
                                                <provenance>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Notices by Renaudot, J. Ascari (1735), and Silvestre de Sacy. Bought by Vansleb in the Orient. From the Bibliothèque Mazarine. Stamps with Peiresc’s cipher. Marginal glosses. Mentions of deaths and reading mark of Buṭrus ibn Dīb al-Ḥalabī dated 1684; purchase mark of Isḥāq Yūsuf al-Sāmirī al-Nābulusī dated AH 962 / 1554-1555 at f. 1; mentions of births and deaths at ff. 358v-359v; note at f. 360 saying that the manuscript was copied three times by Yūḥannā ibn Qaṭā in Paris in 1681.</note>
                                                </provenance>
                                                <origin>
                                                    <origDate calendar="#gregorian" when="1433">1433</origDate>
                                                    <p>Anonymous copy completed in Ḏū l-Qaʿda AH 836 (f. 93).</p>
                                                </origin>
                                            </history>
